LibRaw 0.22.2: wavelet_denoise() under OpenMP allocates with an uninitialised
`size` (the OpenMP branch lost `size = iheight * iwidth;`).

LibRaw issue #842, fixed upstream in a6268d4. Same one-line fix as
thetechgeekko/Spektrafilm-android lib/libraw/patches/0001 (GPL-3.0).
Spektralab-X opens RAWs with threshold = 0, so this path is not taken today;
it is fixed because the OpenMP build compiles it.

--- a/src/postprocessing/postprocessing_aux.cpp
+++ b/src/postprocessing/postprocessing_aux.cpp
@@ -147,6 +147,7 @@
   maximum <<= --scale;
   black <<= scale;
   FORC4 cblack[c] <<= scale;
+  size = iheight * iwidth;
   fimg = (float *)malloc((size * 3 + iheight + iwidth) * sizeof *fimg);
   temp = fimg + size * 3;
   if ((nc = colors) == 3 && filters)
